@tradition big-jigsaw
// The big jigsaw (FX11, 0.92.5 item 16 T4; SW1's weekend pitch, the user's yes 2026-10-24): all Sunday afternoon a huge
// jigsaw of the Wren sits on the observation room's conference table on Deck 1; people drift in and out and add a few
// pieces, Commander Vance always on the edges. The puzzle is decor (DECK_DRESS bigJigsaw) on the table, the seats are
// the table's own (common-room), so Deck 1 is as before other days. A turn is 20 minutes and counts as your puzzles
// hobby (the weekend slot in section 18). Still picture: the week-by-week fill is the large version, not built (ask first).
// Behind WEEKEND_ON.
k: 468
title: The big jigsaw
when: weekly sunday from day 1
at: 13:00-15:30
min: 25
where: 1 room Observation room: common-room
hold: none
who: vance always, quiet-corner 60%, common-room 50%, window-seat 30%, officers 25%, juniors 20%, everyone 12%
anim: read
host: vance
from: vance
ties: decor bigJigsaw

== mail
- The jigsaw is out tomorrow from one, Observation room. Edges are done. Edges are always done first. That is not negotiable.

== ask
- The jigsaw's out on Deck 1. Come and find a piece or two.
- Sky pieces need patient people. Are you patient?

== here
- That one's an edge. Give it here.   #funny
- Sky. All of it is sky. Every piece is sky.   #funny
- There. The hull's nearly joined up.   #warm

== thanks
- You sit at the long table with {host} and find a few pieces of the Wren's hull. The stars can wait for next week.   #warm

== chatter
- The jigsaw's out again on Sunday. Vance has already done the edges in her head.   #funny
- I found the bridge window piece last week. I'm still proud.
- Nobody touches the edges but the Commander.   #funny
